  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Heat builds this week. High confidence in above\nnormal temperatures.\n\nA strong upper ridge will begin to strengthen over the southern\nUnited States by Monday. This ridge will continue to build east\nthrough the week, leading to multiple days of upper 80s to \nupper 90s over the region.\n\nThe heat should peak Wednesday, but remains quite high Thursday\nas well, especially over the Piedmont. Temperatures in the upper \n80s and upper 90s combined with dew points in the mid to upper \n60s will result in heat indices in the lower 100s for parts of \nthe Piedmont as well as the Roanoke urban area during this \nperiod.\n\nThrough Wednesday, and possibly Thursday, rain looks scarce,\nwith a few tiny cells trying to develop in the afternoons and \nearly evenings. Best chance of storms will be along the southern\nBlue Ridge, but strong subsidence under the ridge will prevent\nanything more than shallow convection. Troughing over the\nnortheast by Friday will amplify resulting in a greater chance \nfor rain/storms for the weekend as the strong ridging moves \nwest over the Rockies.",
